IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei3-part4-refunds`

-- Tests of ei3-part4-refunds.l4 (Act ss 95 and 96).
-- Expected values are hand-worked from the text of the section named beside each assertion. Every figure is invented
-- (the rate 1.63% is 0.0163 and the maximum 39,000 here are test figures, not published ones).

§ `The floor and cap helpers`

-- "If that amount is more than $1": exactly the floor is not enough.
#ASSERT `ei3 the refund of` 5 `if it is more than` 1 EQUALS `ei3 a refund is payable` 5
#ASSERT `ei3 the refund of` 1 `if it is more than` 1 EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
#ASSERT `ei3 the refund of` 1.01 `if it is more than` 1 EQUALS `ei3 a refund is payable` 1.01
#ASSERT `ei3 the refund of` 0 `if it is more than` 0 EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
#ASSERT `ei3 the refund` (`ei3 a refund is payable` 700) `capped at` 500 EQUALS `ei3 a refund is payable` 500
#ASSERT `ei3 the refund` (`ei3 a refund is payable` 300) `capped at` 500 EQUALS `ei3 a refund is payable` 300
#ASSERT `ei3 the refund` (`ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`) `capped at` 500 EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
#ASSERT `ei3 the refund` (`ei3 a refund is payable` 300) `capped at the maximum, if there is one,` (JUST 200) EQUALS `ei3 a refund is payable` 200
#ASSERT `ei3 the refund` (`ei3 a refund is payable` 300) `capped at the maximum, if there is one,` NOTHING EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
#ASSERT `s 96 a refund is payable` (`ei3 a refund is payable` 5)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 96 a refund is payable` (`ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`))

§ `s 95 the overpayment`

-- As the text has it, the overpayment is the premiums deducted from the part in excess of the maximum.
#ASSERT `s 95 the overpayment made by the person` 120 EQUALS 120
-- The reading worked from stated facts (fork F-ei3-20). Two employers each paid 30,000 (total 60,000) against a maximum of 39,000
-- at 1.63%: deducted 978 (0.0163 x 60,000); owed on 39,000 is 635.70; the excess is 342.30 (= 0.0163 x 21,000).
#ASSERT `s 95 the premiums deducted in excess of what the maximum allows` 978 60_000 39_000 0.0163 EQUALS 342.3
-- Earnings under the maximum: nothing in excess.
#ASSERT `s 95 the premiums deducted in excess of what the maximum allows` 489 30_000 39_000 0.0163 EQUALS 0
-- The two readings DIFFER when the deductions were not at the full rate: only 900 deducted on 60,000, so the excess is 900 - 635.70 = 264.30,
-- while reading (2), 0.0163 x (60,000 - 39,000), would give 342.30 (it treats the 21,000 above the maximum as if premium had been deducted on it at the full rate).
#ASSERT `s 95 the premiums deducted in excess of what the maximum allows` 900 60_000 39_000 0.0163 EQUALS 264.3
-- Under-deduction (less deducted than the premium on the maximum): no excess, never negative.
#ASSERT `s 95 the premiums deducted in excess of what the maximum allows` 500 60_000 39_000 0.0163 EQUALS 0
-- With only 300 deducted on 60,000, reading (2) would give 342.30, more than was deducted in all; the rule gives 0 (300 is less than the 635.70 owed on the maximum).
#ASSERT `s 95 the premiums deducted in excess of what the maximum allows` 300 60_000 39_000 0.0163 EQUALS 0

§ `s 96(10) and (4.1) application and the bar`

-- The year 2023: three years after its end is 31 December 2026.
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the application for the refund is made in time` TRUE 2023 (YMD 2026 12 31)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 96(10) the application for the refund is made in time` TRUE 2023 (YMD 2027 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 96(10) the application for the refund is made in time` FALSE 2023 (YMD 2025 1 1))
-- The latest year any of the temporary refunds in ss 96(6) to (8.98) is for is 2016: three years after its end is 31 December 2019, so on
-- the consolidation date of this text (30 September 2026) no application for any of them can still be made in time.
#ASSERT `s 96(10) the application for the refund is made in time` TRUE 2016 (YMD 2019 12 31)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 96(10) the application for the refund is made in time` TRUE 2016 (YMD 2020 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 96(10) the application for the refund is made in time` TRUE 2016 (YMD 2026 9 30))
#ASSERT `s 96(4.1) no refund shall be made under subsection (4)` TRUE 2_000.01
#ASSERT NOT (`s 96(4.1) no refund shall be made under subsection (4)` TRUE 2_000)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 96(4.1) no refund shall be made under subsection (4)` FALSE 9_000)

§ `s 96(1) to (3.1) refunds on application`

-- (1) Arguments: overpayment made; payment made when not in insurable employment; the amount; written; year; day of application.
#ASSERT `s 96(1) the refund of the overpayment or of the payment` TRUE FALSE 120 TRUE 2023 (YMD 2026 12 31) EQUALS `ei3 a refund is payable` 120
#ASSERT `s 96(1) the refund of the overpayment or of the payment` FALSE TRUE 75 TRUE 2023 (YMD 2025 5 1) EQUALS `ei3 a refund is payable` 75
#ASSERT `s 96(1) the refund of the overpayment or of the payment` FALSE FALSE 120 TRUE 2023 (YMD 2025 5 1) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
#ASSERT `s 96(1) the refund of the overpayment or of the payment` TRUE FALSE 120 TRUE 2023 (YMD 2027 1 1) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
#ASSERT `s 96(1) the refund of the overpayment or of the payment` TRUE FALSE 120 FALSE 2023 (YMD 2025 5 1) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
-- (2) Arguments: amount deducted or paid; a decision found it excessive; the excess; applies in writing; decision communicated on; application on.
-- Decision communicated 1 March 2026: 30 days after is 31 March 2026.
#ASSERT `s 96(2) the refund after a decision on an appeal` TRUE TRUE 80 TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 31) EQUALS `ei3 a refund is payable` 80
#ASSERT `s 96(2) the refund after a decision on an appeal` TRUE TRUE 80 TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 4 1) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
#ASSERT `s 96(2) the refund after a decision on an appeal` TRUE FALSE 80 TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 2) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
#ASSERT `s 96(2) the refund after a decision on an appeal` TRUE TRUE 80 FALSE (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 2) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
#ASSERT `s 96(2) the refund after a decision on an appeal` FALSE TRUE 80 TRUE (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 2) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
-- (3) the Minister MAY refund: applies, satisfies the Minister, within three years after the end of the year.
#ASSERT `s 96(3) the Minister may refund the excess amount or the amount that should not have been deducted or paid` TRUE TRUE 2023 (YMD 2026 12 31)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 96(3) the Minister may refund the excess amount or the amount that should not have been deducted or paid` TRUE TRUE 2023 (YMD 2027 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 96(3) the Minister may refund the excess amount or the amount that should not have been deducted or paid` TRUE FALSE 2023 (YMD 2025 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 96(3) the Minister may refund the excess amount or the amount that should not have been deducted or paid` FALSE TRUE 2023 (YMD 2025 1 1))
#ASSERT `s 96(3.1) the Minister may refund the amount to the employer` TRUE 2023 (YMD 2026 12 31)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 96(3.1) the Minister may refund the amount to the employer` TRUE 2023 (YMD 2027 1 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 96(3.1) the Minister may refund the amount to the employer` FALSE 2023 (YMD 2025 1 1))

§ `s 96(4) to (5.1) the $2,000 rules`

-- (4) Arguments: insurable earnings; aggregate deducted; also self-employed (Part VII.1); total earnings under Part VII.1; written; year; day.
#ASSERT `s 96(4) the refund of premiums on insurable earnings of not more than $2,000` 2_000 32.6 FALSE 0 TRUE 2023 (YMD 2025 3 1) EQUALS `ei3 a refund is payable` 32.6
#ASSERT `s 96(4) the refund of premiums on insurable earnings of not more than $2,000` 0 0.5 FALSE 0 TRUE 2023 (YMD 2025 3 1) EQUALS `ei3 a refund is payable` 0.5
#ASSERT `s 96(4) the refund of premiums on insurable earnings of not more than $2,000` 2_000.01 32.6 FALSE 0 TRUE 2023 (YMD 2025 3 1) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
-- (4.1): self-employed with total earnings over $2,000 gets no refund under (4); at exactly $2,000 total, the refund stands.
#ASSERT `s 96(4) the refund of premiums on insurable earnings of not more than $2,000` 1_500 24.45 TRUE 2_000.01 TRUE 2023 (YMD 2025 3 1) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
#ASSERT `s 96(4) the refund of premiums on insurable earnings of not more than $2,000` 1_500 24.45 TRUE 2_000 TRUE 2023 (YMD 2025 3 1) EQUALS `ei3 a refund is payable` 24.45
-- (10): an application out of time, or not in writing, gets nothing.
#ASSERT `s 96(4) the refund of premiums on insurable earnings of not more than $2,000` 1_500 24.45 FALSE 0 TRUE 2023 (YMD 2027 1 1) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
#ASSERT `s 96(4) the refund of premiums on insurable earnings of not more than $2,000` 1_500 24.45 FALSE 0 FALSE 2023 (YMD 2025 3 1) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
-- (5) Arguments: self-employed (Part VII.1); IE; P; written; year; day. Refund is 2,000 - (IE - P) if more than $1.
#ASSERT `s 96(5) the refund of the shortfall below $2,000` FALSE 2_100 150 TRUE 2023 (YMD 2025 3 1) EQUALS `ei3 a refund is payable` 50
#ASSERT `s 96(5) the refund of the shortfall below $2,000` FALSE 2_100 101.5 TRUE 2023 (YMD 2025 3 1) EQUALS `ei3 a refund is payable` 1.5
-- Exactly $1 is not "more than $1"; IE - P of exactly 2,000 is not "less than 2,000"; IE of exactly 2,000 is not "more than 2,000".
#ASSERT `s 96(5) the refund of the shortfall below $2,000` FALSE 2_100 101 TRUE 2023 (YMD 2025 3 1) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
#ASSERT `s 96(5) the refund of the shortfall below $2,000` FALSE 2_100 100 TRUE 2023 (YMD 2025 3 1) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
#ASSERT `s 96(5) the refund of the shortfall below $2,000` FALSE 2_000 0 TRUE 2023 (YMD 2025 3 1) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
#ASSERT `s 96(5) the refund of the shortfall below $2,000` FALSE 3_000 50 TRUE 2023 (YMD 2025 3 1) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
#ASSERT `s 96(5) the refund of the shortfall below $2,000` TRUE 2_100 150 TRUE 2023 (YMD 2025 3 1) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
#ASSERT `s 96(5) the refund of the shortfall below $2,000` FALSE 2_100 150 TRUE 2023 (YMD 2027 1 1) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
-- (5.1) Arguments: has insurable earnings; also self-employed; TE; aggregate deducted; the Part VII.1 premium; written; year; day.
-- TE 2,500, deducted 60, SE premium 500: TP 560, TE - TP 1,940; (b) is 60; lesser of 60 and 60 is 60.
#ASSERT `s 96(5.1) the refund of the shortfall below $2,000 for a person who is also self-employed` TRUE TRUE 2_500 60 500 TRUE 2023 (YMD 2025 3 1) EQUALS `ei3 a refund is payable` 60
-- Deducted 100, SE premium 450: TP 550, TE - TP 1,950, (b) is 50, (a) is 100: the lesser, 50.
#ASSERT `s 96(5.1) the refund of the shortfall below $2,000 for a person who is also self-employed` TRUE TRUE 2_500 100 450 TRUE 2023 (YMD 2025 3 1) EQUALS `ei3 a refund is payable` 50
-- Deducted 30, SE premium 600: TP 630, TE - TP 1,870, (b) is 130, (a) is 30: the lesser, 30.
#ASSERT `s 96(5.1) the refund of the shortfall below $2,000 for a person who is also self-employed` TRUE TRUE 2_500 30 600 TRUE 2023 (YMD 2025 3 1) EQUALS `ei3 a refund is payable` 30
-- The gates: more than $1 (here (b) is exactly 1), TE over 2,000, TE - TP under 2,000, both kinds of earnings, in time.
#ASSERT `s 96(5.1) the refund of the shortfall below $2,000 for a person who is also self-employed` TRUE TRUE 2_500 100 401 TRUE 2023 (YMD 2025 3 1) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
#ASSERT `s 96(5.1) the refund of the shortfall below $2,000 for a person who is also self-employed` TRUE TRUE 2_000 0 0 TRUE 2023 (YMD 2025 3 1) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
#ASSERT `s 96(5.1) the refund of the shortfall below $2,000 for a person who is also self-employed` TRUE TRUE 3_000 60 500 TRUE 2023 (YMD 2025 3 1) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
#ASSERT `s 96(5.1) the refund of the shortfall below $2,000 for a person who is also self-employed` TRUE FALSE 2_500 60 500 TRUE 2023 (YMD 2025 3 1) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
#ASSERT `s 96(5.1) the refund of the shortfall below $2,000 for a person who is also self-employed` FALSE TRUE 2_500 60 500 TRUE 2023 (YMD 2025 3 1) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
#ASSERT `s 96(5.1) the refund of the shortfall below $2,000 for a person who is also self-employed` TRUE TRUE 2_500 60 500 TRUE 2023 (YMD 2027 1 1) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`

§ `s 96(6) to (9) the 1997 and 1998 employer refunds`

#ASSERT `s 96(8.1) the employer's premium in 1996` 30_000 12_000 EQUALS 42_000
#ASSERT `s 96(7.1) P1 for subsections (6) and (7)` 40_000 TRUE EQUALS 40_000
#ASSERT `s 96(7.1) P1 for subsections (6) and (7)` 40_000 FALSE EQUALS 0
-- (8): under $50,000 the cap is $10,000; from $50,000 to under $60,000 it is $60,000 minus the 1996 premium; $60,000 or more: not covered.
#ASSERT `s 96(8) the maximum refund under subsection (6) or (7)` 49_999 EQUALS JUST 10_000
#ASSERT `s 96(8) the maximum refund under subsection (6) or (7)` 50_000 EQUALS JUST 10_000
#ASSERT `s 96(8) the maximum refund under subsection (6) or (7)` 55_000 EQUALS JUST 5_000
#ASSERT `s 96(8) the maximum refund under subsection (6) or (7)` 59_999 EQUALS JUST 1
#ASSERT `s 96(8) the maximum refund under subsection (6) or (7)` 60_000 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (6) Arguments: P1; required to pay in 1996; P2; written; day of application. P2 - (P1 + 250), more than $1, up to the cap.
#ASSERT `s 96(6) the refund of part of the employer's premium for 1997` 40_000 TRUE 45_000 TRUE (YMD 2000 12 31) EQUALS `ei3 a refund is payable` 4_750
#ASSERT `s 96(6) the refund of part of the employer's premium for 1997` 40_000 TRUE 45_000 TRUE (YMD 2001 1 1) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
-- P1 55,000, P2 70,000: 70,000 - 55,250 = 14,750, capped at 60,000 - 55,000 = 5,000.
#ASSERT `s 96(6) the refund of part of the employer's premium for 1997` 55_000 TRUE 70_000 TRUE (YMD 1999 5 5) EQUALS `ei3 a refund is payable` 5_000
-- P1 59,999 (cap 1): 70,000 - 60,249 = 9,751, capped at 1.
#ASSERT `s 96(6) the refund of part of the employer's premium for 1997` 59_999 TRUE 70_000 TRUE (YMD 1999 5 5) EQUALS `ei3 a refund is payable` 1
-- P1 of 60,000 or more: no refund at all. P1 of 50,000: cap 10,000, formula gives 19,750.
#ASSERT `s 96(6) the refund of part of the employer's premium for 1997` 60_000 TRUE 90_000 TRUE (YMD 1999 5 5) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
#ASSERT `s 96(6) the refund of part of the employer's premium for 1997` 50_000 TRUE 70_000 TRUE (YMD 1999 5 5) EQUALS `ei3 a refund is payable` 10_000
-- No 1996 premium was required: P1 is zero (7.1), so P2 of 1,000 gives 750.
#ASSERT `s 96(6) the refund of part of the employer's premium for 1997` 99_999 FALSE 1_000 TRUE (YMD 1999 5 5) EQUALS `ei3 a refund is payable` 750
-- The $1 gate: P2 - (P1 + 250) of exactly 1 is not more than 1; of 2 it is.
#ASSERT `s 96(6) the refund of part of the employer's premium for 1997` 10_000 TRUE 10_251 TRUE (YMD 1999 5 5) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
#ASSERT `s 96(6) the refund of part of the employer's premium for 1997` 10_000 TRUE 10_252 TRUE (YMD 1999 5 5) EQUALS `ei3 a refund is payable` 2
#ASSERT `s 96(6) the refund of part of the employer's premium for 1997` 40_000 TRUE 45_000 FALSE (YMD 1999 5 5) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
-- (7): [P2 - (P1 + 250)] / 4 for 1998. P1 40,000, P2 48,000: (48,000 - 40,250) / 4 = 1,937.50.
#ASSERT `s 96(7) the refund of part of the employer's premium for 1998` 40_000 TRUE 48_000 TRUE (YMD 2001 12 31) EQUALS `ei3 a refund is payable` 1_937.5
#ASSERT `s 96(7) the refund of part of the employer's premium for 1998` 40_000 TRUE 48_000 TRUE (YMD 2002 1 1) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
-- P1 55,000, P2 100,000: (100,000 - 55,250) / 4 = 11,187.50, capped at 5,000.
#ASSERT `s 96(7) the refund of part of the employer's premium for 1998` 55_000 TRUE 100_000 TRUE (YMD 2000 5 5) EQUALS `ei3 a refund is payable` 5_000
#ASSERT `s 96(7) the refund of part of the employer's premium for 1998` 60_000 TRUE 100_000 TRUE (YMD 2000 5 5) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
-- (9)
#ASSERT `s 96(9) the associated employers are considered a single employer for subsections (6) to (8.4)` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 96(9) the associated employers are considered a single employer for subsections (6) to (8.4)` FALSE)

§ `s 96(8.2) to (8.6) the 1999 and 2000 refunds`

-- Premium rate 2.50%, so 1.4 times it is 3.5% (0.035). (E2 - E1) x 0.035: 20,000 x 0.035 = 700.
#ASSERT `s 96(8.2) the refund of the employer's premium for 1999` 100_000 120_000 0.025 TRUE (YMD 2002 12 31) EQUALS `ei3 a refund is payable` 700
#ASSERT `s 96(8.2) the refund of the employer's premium for 1999` 100_000 120_000 0.025 TRUE (YMD 2003 1 1) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
-- Smaller earnings in 1999 than 1998: a negative amount is not "more than $1". An amount of $0.70 is not either.
#ASSERT `s 96(8.2) the refund of the employer's premium for 1999` 120_000 100_000 0.025 TRUE (YMD 2001 1 1) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
#ASSERT `s 96(8.2) the refund of the employer's premium for 1999` 100_000 100_020 0.025 TRUE (YMD 2001 1 1) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
-- 2000: E1 is still the 1998 figure. (130,000 - 100,000) x 0.035 = 1,050.
#ASSERT `s 96(8.3) the refund of the employer's premium for 2000` 100_000 130_000 0.025 TRUE (YMD 2003 12 31) EQUALS `ei3 a refund is payable` 1_050
#ASSERT `s 96(8.3) the refund of the employer's premium for 2000` 100_000 130_000 0.025 TRUE (YMD 2004 1 1) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
-- (8.4) Arguments: the refund; it is determined the employer unduly terminated or changed employment; the sum of reduction, if reduced.
#ASSERT `s 96(8.4) the refund after elimination or reduction` (`ei3 a refund is payable` 700) FALSE NOTHING EQUALS `ei3 a refund is payable` 700
#ASSERT `s 96(8.4) the refund after elimination or reduction` (`ei3 a refund is payable` 700) TRUE NOTHING EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
#ASSERT `s 96(8.4) the refund after elimination or reduction` (`ei3 a refund is payable` 700) TRUE (JUST 200) EQUALS `ei3 a refund is payable` 500
#ASSERT `s 96(8.4) the refund after elimination or reduction` (`ei3 a refund is payable` 700) TRUE (JUST 700) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
#ASSERT `s 96(8.4) the refund after elimination or reduction` (`ei3 a refund is payable` 700) TRUE (JUST 800) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
#ASSERT `s 96(8.4) the refund after elimination or reduction` (`ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`) TRUE (JUST 200) EQUALS `ei3 no refund is payable under the provision`
#ASSERT `s 96(8.5) the Minister shall notify the employer as if issuing a notice of assessment` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 96(8.5) the Minister shall notify the employer as if issuing a notice of assessment` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 96(8.6) the employer is determined to have unduly terminated or changed the employment` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 96(8.6) the employer is determined to have unduly terminated or changed the employment` FALSE)

§ `s 96(8.7) to (8.98) the small business refunds`

